<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	RoR is built with plain CMake rather than Xcode, so nothing supplies an
	entitlements file at all.  This deliberately EMPTY dictionary exists only
	so that codesign embeds an entitlements blob - and, with
	--generate-entitlement-der, its DER form - exactly the way the one bundle
	in this repository that is known to install was signed:

	    codesign --force --sign - --entitlements Free.entitlements \
	             --generate-entitlement-der "$APP"

	A free Apple ID cannot carry extra entitlements, so there is nothing to
	put in here.  The signatures that actually authorise the app are added by
	whoever sideloads the IPA (ESIGN, Sideloadly, SideStore, ...).
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
